<title>UK: GOLF-LEADING RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Justin Leonard, winner of the</p>
<p>British Open at the weekend, jumps six places to 13th in the</p>
<p>world rankings issued on Monday.</p>
<p>Tiger Woods stays clear at the top while Greg Norman regains</p>
<p>the second spot he lost to South Africa's Ernie Els last week.</p>
<p>Top 20:</p>
<p>  1. Tiger Woods (U.S.)	    11.00 points average</p>
<p>  2. Greg Norman (Australia)     10.28</p>
<p>  3. Ernie Els (South Africa)    10.20</p>
<p>  4. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)  9.77</p>
<p>  5. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	  9.52</p>
<p>  6. Tom Lehman (U.S.)		8.55</p>
<p>  7. Steve Elkington (Australia)  8.36</p>
<p>  8. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	  7.91</p>
<p>  9. Mark O'Meara (U.S.)	    7.63</p>
<p> 10. Phil Mickelson (U.S.)	  7.24</p>
<p> 11. Brad Faxon (U.S.)		6.80</p>
<p> 12. Fred Couples (U.S.)	    6.77</p>
<p> 13. Justin Leonard (U.S.)	  6.77</p>
<p> 14. Nick Faldo (Britain)	   6.73</p>
<p> 15. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)     6.63</p>
<p> 16. Scott Hoch (U.S.)		6.60</p>
<p> 17. Davis Love III (U.S.)	  5.72</p>
<p> 18. Tom Watson (U.S.)		5.30</p>
<p> 19. Ian Woosnam (Britain)	  5.30</p>
<p> 20. Bernhard Langer (Germany)    5.14</p>
